    <worksheet name='Pedestrian &amp; Cyclist Map'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Which locations should SDOT prioritize to protect pedestrians and cyclists?</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Aurora Ave N holds two of the top four spots</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>, including the single worst location. There’s also a pattern in northwest Seattle, where three locations on 15th Ave NW, 15th Ave W, and 24th Ave NW made the list. SDOT should start pedestrian and cyclist safety upgrades on Aurora, followed by the downtown intersections, Rainier Ave S, and the northwest corridors.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources>
            <datasource caption='SDOT_Collisions_Clean' name='federated.0vp66e207341pz1ftvevs1bo577n' />
